requirement CHILD
title: Derived child behavior
allocation: Subsystem
statement:
  The subsystem shall provide the behavior allocated by the parent requirement.
rationale:
  The child identifies a separately reviewable implementation responsibility.
decomposes: TOP
end requirement

requirement LEAF
title: Leaf timing behavior
statement:
  The component shall complete the behavior within the interval defined by:

  math latex
    t_{complete} - t_{start} \le 100\,\mathrm{ms}
  end math

  The interval uses a monotonic time source.
source: TEST-SOURCE, revision A, section 4.2
decomposes: CHILD
decomposes: TOP
end requirement

requirement TOP
title: Top-level behavior
allocation: System
statement:
  The system shall provide the required externally observable behavior.

  The behavior shall remain available throughout normal operation.
rationale:
  The top-level requirement defines the user-visible outcome independently of implementation.
source: TEST-SOURCE, revision A, section 4
end requirement
